# Pure SaaS Windsurf Rules
# Universal UI/UX Design System & Anti-Slop Discipline

When modifying or generating frontend components, styling, or layouts:
1. Universal Command: Use `/pure-saas [any request]` or copy from `prompts/pure-saas.md` as the default. Automatically coordinates design, implementation, components, tokens, motion, accessibility, responsiveness, performance, security, and verification.
2. Specialist Commands (see prompts/ directory):
   - design: Establish or update persistent DESIGN.md specification (prompts/design.md)
   - polish: Raise visual craft, typography, and micro-interactions (prompts/polish.md)
   - review: Quality audit across bugs, security, accessibility, and performance (prompts/review.md)
   - reference: Reverse-engineer visual reference via browser DevTools (prompts/reference.md)
   - responsive: Cross-device layout optimization across mobile, tablet, and desktop (prompts/responsive.md)
3. Anti-Slop Discipline: Prohibit unapproved purple/cyan gradient text, excessive glassmorphism, monotonous 3-column cards, and emoji icons.
4. Semantic Tokens: Bind all styling to tokens in DESIGN.md. Validate with `node scripts/pure-saas.mjs validate DESIGN.md`.
5. Non-Regression: Preserve 100% of existing backend APIs, server actions, and database schemas.
